INT. CABLE CAR CABIN - ALPINE GORGE - NIGHT

A glass box suspended over blackness. Wind buffets it. Lights of a village glimmer far below.

DR. SOLVEIG RASMUSSEN, 40s, grips a metal briefcase. Opposite her, AGENT KAZIMIR DOBRYNIN, 50s, sits calm, a pistol in his lap. LUCIEN FAUREAU, 30s, the operator, huddles near the control panel. TAMARA QUINN, 20s, a journalist with a camera, crouches by the door.

Static from the radio. The cabin lurches and stops.

SOLVEIG
Why did we stop?

LUCIEN
Wind. It trips the brake.

KAZIMIR
The wind did not trip it.

Lucien checks the panel. Tamara lifts the camera and starts filming. Kazimir slides a hand over the lens.

KAZIMIR (CONT'D)
No.

TAMARA
Public interest.

KAZIMIR
Private interest. Mine.

Solveig edges the briefcase behind her knees. Kazimir notices. He raises the pistol, not at her, but at the ceiling. A single shot cracks the roof light. Wind shrieks in. Lucien dives for the floor. Tamara drops the camera. It skids to the door and tumbles out of a gap. Solveig lunges for the pistol, and Kazimir catches her wrist. They struggle. The cabin swings.

SOLVEIG
Let go.

KAZIMIR
The case, Doctor.

SOLVEIG
It's not yours.

KAZIMIR
It was never yours.

Lucien crawls toward the panel. Tamara grabs his ankle.

TAMARA
What are you doing?

LUCIEN
Restarting the brake.

TAMARA
Don't. He'll kill us.

LUCIEN
He'll kill us anyway.

He hits a lever. The cabin lurches forward. Kazimir loses his balance. Solveig wrenches the pistol free, and it clatters across the floor. Tamara scoops it up and aims at Kazimir with both hands.

TAMARA (CONT'D)
Sit down.

KAZIMIR
You will not shoot.

TAMARA
Try me.

Kazimir sits. Solveig flips the case open: nothing inside but a photograph. Lucien stares at it. Kazimir smiles.

SOLVEIG
You wanted a photograph?

KAZIMIR
I wanted the man in it.

Solveig turns it over. A name. Her own. The cabin glides on into the dark.

LUCIEN
(to the room)
We're ten minutes from the station.

TAMARA
Then we have ten minutes.

KAZIMIR
For what?

TAMARA
For you to talk.

Kazimir says nothing. The wind drops. Solveig steadies herself on the rail and holds the photograph up to the light. The faces blur. The village grows closer below.

SOLVEIG
Who sent you?

KAZIMIR
The man who took your picture.

SOLVEIG
My father took that picture.

KAZIMIR
Yes.

Tamara's grip on the pistol tightens. Lucien checks the panel. The cabin hums. A light on the dock ahead flashes red.

LUCIEN
Station's alerted.

TAMARA
They'll be waiting.

Kazimir shrugs. Solveig folds the photograph into her coat. The cabin glides into the dock. The door slides open. Armed uniformed men fill the platform.

KAZIMIR
Doctor. Ask them whose uniforms those are.

Solveig looks. Her face falls. She takes a step back.

SOLVEIG
Those are my father's.
